        'excerpt'    => 'A 2027 COLA chart with new check amounts, plus spousal, SSDI and SSI figures and what the raise means state by state.',
        'answer'     => 'The Social Security 2027 benefit increase is 3.6% in every state, because the COLA is set nationally. A $1,500 benefit becomes $1,554 and a $2,000 benefit becomes $2,072. What differs by state is the average benefit, which follows local earnings, and whether your state taxes benefits; eight states still did for 2025.',
        'takeaways'  => [
